{"reference":"Proverbs 17","book":"Proverbs","chapter":17,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Justice and Material Outcomes","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Proverbs 17:23 condemns a bribe used to distort justice. This warning belongs within a wider set of Proverbs sayings that connect material outcomes with diligence and choice while also condemning practices that exploit others or deny justice. The relationship between these themes is debated, so the chapter should not be read as offering a simple rule that wealth or poverty always proves a person's character.","verse_refs":["Proverbs 17:23"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_proverbs_017_7f2dae68a71d7a58bb3451e0"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}